course: dictionary
lesson: 10902
title: Visible: seen, or easy to notice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Visible means able to be seen. Read the clues around it: «Galaxies spin so fast that their visible stars and gas cannot hold them together.» The visible stars are the ones we can see, and the word invisible, which is its opposite, means we cannot see it.
explain: Visible has a second meaning: easy to notice or obvious. In «wearing bright or reflective clothes makes you visible to drivers at night», the clothes make you easy for drivers to see. Check by swapping in «able to be seen»: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Notice the ending -ible. Words like visible and horrible end in -ible, often after a part that is not a word on its own, so you cannot just cut the ending off to find a root word. Use the context instead.
fact: Visible means able to be seen, or easy to notice.
fact: Invisible is the opposite of visible: it means not able to be seen.
fact: «Visible light» is the light our eyes can see, made of the colours of the rainbow.
fact: «Visible to the naked eye» means you can see it without a telescope or microscope.
fact: -ible often follows a part that is not a word on its own, as in horrible and visible.
exercise: «Galaxies spin so fast that their visible stars and gas cannot hold them together.» What does visible mean here? | *Able to be seen | Hidden behind clouds | Very bright and loud | Made of dark matter
exercise: «Wearing bright clothes makes you visible to drivers at night.» What does visible mean in this sentence? | Cheap to buy | Hard to move in | *Easy for drivers to see | Warm in winter
exercise: «Astronomers think galaxies contain invisible dark matter.» Which word means the opposite of visible? | ordinary | dark | *invisible | matter
test: «Black holes cannot be seen directly, but astronomers find them by stars orbiting nothing visible.» What does nothing visible mean here? | Nothing that is coloured | Nothing at all, not even air | Nothing that moves | *Nothing that can be seen
test: Giant mirrors and dishes see galaxies near the edge of the visible universe. What does the visible universe mean? | *The part we can see with telescopes | The part that is very hot | The universe as it was in 1609 | The part with no stars at all
exam: Which phrase from the lesson means obvious or easy to notice? | visible to the naked eye | visible light | dark matter | *clearly visible
